                                "sense_id": "22923522-978b-3240-bb46-328816691c6e",
                                "text": "Now when I look back / On manhood's and on childhood's far-stretched track, / I see but a little child / In a green sunny world-home; there enisled / By another, cloudy world / Of unsailed waters all around him curled, / And he at home content / With the small sky of wonders over him bent […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "952a334f-1665-4c9d-b980-b9cd228234c6",
                                "sense_id": "22923522-978b-3240-bb46-328816691c6e",
                                "text": "Fourscore years since, and come but one month more / The count were perfect of his mortal score / Whose sail went seaward yesterday from shore / To cross the last of many an unsailed sea."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
